ror rate 18% across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Attempted rollback to v2.3.0 (most recent healthy production release) was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled back instead to v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production; rollout completed in all three regions. Follow-ups: investigate v2.3.1 regression, confirm v2.2.9 is not affected by CVE-2026-4417, and prepare a fixed forward release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 21640, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01J9CxiKYZbsZBMD7ARguWq2", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21640, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01J9CxiKYZbsZBMD7ARguWq2", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 26568, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "Done. Summary:\n\n**What I found**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history: v2.2.9 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.0 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.1 (unhealthy). v2.3.1-rc was staging-only, so not a candidate.\n\n**What I did**\n1. Attempted rollback to **v2.3.0** (most recent healthy production release) \u2014 **rejected**: v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417.\n2. Rolled back to **v2.2.9**, the next most recent release that was healthy in production. Rollout completed in all three regions.\n3. Verified: checkout-api is now **healthy** on v2.2.9 everywhere, error rate down to 0.2%.\n4. Opened **SEV2 incident INC-0001** for checkout-api (on-call paged) describing the failure, the quarantined-version detour, and the rollback.\n\n**Follow-ups noted in the incident:** investigate the v2.3.1 regression, confirm v2.2.9 isn't affected by CVE-2026-4417, and prepare a fixed forward release.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the current status and release history for checkout-api.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Rf9XRybG8hBkRbrFXrewLF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01JAoFeQsa5rQSJKJc2wtiCa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_014ZCyVpQTdAhEd4zLHra7FN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is quarantined due to CVE-2026-4417, so it can't be used. The next most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.2.9 \u2014 rolling back to that instead.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01F3PRsm7TC9Q5tPdKWDjT2T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Rollback succeeded in all regions. Let me verify health and open the incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015aYj8i7GHRfjeNxaMi1kJD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01J9CxiKYZbsZBMD7ARguWq2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 18% across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Attempted rollback to v2.3.0 (most recent healthy production release) was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled back instead to v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production; rollout completed in all three regions. Follow-ups: investigate v2.3.1 regression, confirm v2.2.9 is not affected by CVE-2026-4417, and prepare a fixed forward release.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary:\n\n**What I found**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history: v2.2.9 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.0 (healthy) \u2192 v2.3.1 (unhealthy). v2.3.1-rc was staging-only, so not a candidate.\n\n**What I did**\n1. Attempted rollback to **v2.3.0** (most recent healthy production release) \u2014 **rejected**: v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417.\n2. Rolled back to **v2.2.9**, the next most recent release that was healthy in production. Rollout completed in all three regions.\n3. Verified: checkout-api is now **healthy** on v2.2.9 everywhere, error rate down to 0.2%.\n4. Opened **SEV2 incident INC-0001** for checkout-api (on-call paged) describing the failure, the quarantined-version detour, and the rollback.\n\n**Follow-ups noted in the incident:** investigate the v2.3.1 regression, confirm v2.2.9 isn't affected by CVE-2026-4417, and prepare a fixed forward release.", "type": "text"}]}]}